From: Fix Dawn WebGPU crash on GLES 2.0 drivers
Subject: Guard glGetStringi in Dawn OpenGL backend for GLES 2.0

Dawn's OpenGL backend (WebGPU) has its own GL function dispatch table,
separate from Chromium's ui/gl/ dispatch. When enumerating OpenGL ES
adapters via CollectDawnInfo, it calls LoadOpenGLESProcs which
conditionally loads GL functions by version. On GLES 2.0 drivers
(e.g. Vivante GC NanoUltra on i.MX8MM), glGetStringi is not loaded
because it requires GLES 3.0+. The function pointer stays NULL.

InitializeSupportedGLExtensions() then calls GetStringi unconditionally,
causing a SIGSEGV (NULL function pointer dereference).

GDB backtrace:
  #0  0x0000000000000000 in ?? ()
  #1  dawn::native::opengl::OpenGLFunctionsBase::InitializeSupportedGLExtensions
      at OpenGLFunctionsBase_autogen.cpp:1215
  #2  dawn::native::opengl::OpenGLFunctionsBase::LoadOpenGLESProcs
      (majorVersion=2, minorVersion=0) at OpenGLFunctionsBase_autogen.cpp:392

Fix by checking GetStringi for NULL and falling back to the legacy
glGetString(GL_EXTENSIONS) which returns a space-separated string.
This is the standard approach for querying extensions on pre-3.0 GL.

Note: This is a Jinja2 template file. The generated autogen .cpp has
different line numbers but the same logic.

Tested on: NXP i.MX8MM EVK with Chromium 129.0.6668.100
(Vivante GC NanoUltra, GLES 2.0 only)

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://crbug.com]

---

--- a/third_party/dawn/generator/templates/opengl/OpenGLFunctionsBase.cpp
+++ b/third_party/dawn/generator/templates/opengl/OpenGLFunctionsBase.cpp
@@ -93,6 +93,30 @@
 #endif

 void OpenGLFunctionsBase::InitializeSupportedGLExtensions() {
+    // glGetStringi requires OpenGL 3.0+ / OpenGL ES 3.0+.
+    // On older contexts (e.g. GLES 2.0) it is not loaded and the function
+    // pointer is NULL.  Fall back to the legacy glGetString(GL_EXTENSIONS)
+    // which returns a space-separated list.
+    if (GetStringi == nullptr) {
+        const char* extensions =
+            reinterpret_cast<const char*>(GetString(GL_EXTENSIONS));
+        if (extensions != nullptr) {
+            const char* p = extensions;
+            while (*p != '\0') {
+                while (*p == ' ')
+                    ++p;
+                if (*p == '\0')
+                    break;
+                const char* end = p;
+                while (*end != ' ' && *end != '\0')
+                    ++end;
+                mSupportedGLExtensionsSet.insert(std::string(p, end));
+                p = end;
+            }
+        }
+        return;
+    }
+
     int32_t numExtensions;
     GetIntegerv(GL_NUM_EXTENSIONS, &numExtensions);

